    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d603">

                <pb facs="0715" n="1549" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/799</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-12T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 12, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1959. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 1398. Your 1596, Embassy 2513, October 5. We adopt the recommendation set
                    forth in your cablegram and are disposed to postpone negotiations for separate
                    agreements until conclusion of general agreement, provided no great delay
                    results. We concur in the belief that there should be uniformity. In the
                    meantime we will continue to make consignments to the N[etherlands] O[versea]
                    T[rust].</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
